or good tv however he lacked  even basic gold mining experience his  first mining season ended with a yield  of just under 15 ounces but hoffman was  undeterred  we haven't accomplished our goal we've  proven that you can still do stuff like  this here in america over the course of  the next two seasons he and his team  improved greatly then came a disastrous  trip to guyana in season 4 where hoffman  and his crew were utterly defeated by  the south american jungle mining just  two ounces of gold before an  unsuccessful pivot to diamond mining  after returning to the yukon in season 5  hoffman's skill and attitude recovered  in season six he mined a personal best  3032 ounces after failed attempts to  open minds in colorado and his home  state of oregon hoffman left gold rush  in the mining industry altogether after  season eight he would finish the series  with a total yield of 8039 ounces of  gold worth 14.3 million dollars  colorful dutch miner tony beatz first  appeared on the show in season 2 when  the hoffman crew relocated to dawson  city yukon before long he became a fan  favorite with his wild beard and foul  mouth demeanor he was seemingly made to  become a breakout reality tv star it  helped that he was by far the most  experienced minor of the show's main  cast for tony this is a bad week 220  ounces of gold worth about 350 thousand  dollars  his brusque way of doing business has  also earned him long-standing beasts  with co-stars rick ness and parker  schnabel starting out in season five  with an ambitious quest to get a 75 year  old dredge mine up and running beats has  been running his cruise with the  assistance of his wife minnie and his  daughter monica like the hoffman crew  his seasons have been up and down  however thanks to his prior experience  in the industry when beats has a good  season he brings in a lot of gold to  date beats his mind a total of 16 261  ounces of gold were 28.9 million dollars  in season seven he managed the largest  single gold cleanup in the show's  history to that point but his personal  best came in season 9 with 4 400 ounces  beets would be the most consistently  successful miner on the show if not for  the last name on this list  when it comes to gold yields parker  schnabel is head and shoulders above the  rest schnabel joined the gold rush cast  as a teenager working on one of his  grandfather's old claims throughout his  career on the show schnabel has mined an  incredible 39 910 ounces or 67.8 million  dollars  not only has schnabel found success as a  minor he is also the longest-running  most consistent star of gold rush  starting as a 16 year old overcharging  the hoffman crew for firewood schnabel  emerged as not just a camera friendly  presence but a mining prodigy who saved  the hoffman crew from their own  incompetence on more than one occasion  inspired by his grandfather john a  lifelong alaskan miner schnabel  excavated the big nugget creek mine on  his own in season 2. while that claim  yielded just 34 ounces he very quickly  moved on to bigger and better things  since season 4 he has been the top  earner of each season yielding a record  7509 ounces in season 11. through the  years he has faced setbacks and  hardships including the death of his  grandfather but has managed to persevere  and thrive both in the mountains and on  camera  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  gold rush are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]

